From: Thomas Roos <thomas@exein.io>
Subject: [PATCH] scsi: ufs: spacemit: k3: set UniPro HCLKDIV like vendor driver

The vendor driver ends its UniPro init sequence with UFS_HCLKDIV_REG =
0xFC; the submitted driver defines the register but never sets it, so
UniPro timers run with the reset default. It also clears
ANA_HSGEAR_CTRL_ATTR after a power mode change, which the vendor driver
does not do. Match the vendor driver in both places.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Thomas Roos <thomas@exein.io>
---
--- a/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-spacemit.c
+++ b/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-spacemit.c
@@ -235,6 +235,8 @@
 		/* RX garbage cnt = 32 SI */
 		{ UIC_ARG_MIB_SEL(0x00F2, UIC_ARG_MPHY_RX_GEN_SEL_INDEX(0)), 0x9F },
 		{ UIC_ARG_MIB_SEL(0x00F2, UIC_ARG_MPHY_RX_GEN_SEL_INDEX(1)), 0x9F },
+		/* host clock divider, as in the vendor driver */
+		{ UIC_ARG_MIB(UFS_HCLKDIV_REG), 0xFC },
 	};
 
 	return ufs_spacemit_dme_set(hba, setup_attrs, ARRAY_SIZE(setup_attrs));
@@ -370,8 +372,6 @@
 			return ret;
 
 		dev_dbg(hba->dev, "M-PHY PLL locked after power mode change\n");
-		/* Set ANA_HSGEAR_CTRL_ATTR back to default value */
-		ufshcd_dme_set(hba, UIC_ARG_MIB(ANA_HSGEAR_CTRL_ATTR), 0x00);
 		break;
 	default:
 		return -EINVAL;
